I return to the flat.
I open my laptop.
I make a video call to Mexico.
My brother Diego answers the call.
"Hello Maya, are you well?" Diego asks.
"I am well, Diego," I say.
"I have a very good new desk at the office."
I tell him this proudly.
"Do you have an Indian phone number now?" he asks.
"Yes, I have an Indian number now," I say.
"It works well."
"Is it hot in Kochi now?" he asks.
"No, it is not hot here now," I say.
"The weather in January is very good."
"Is Lola well?" I ask again.
"Yes, Lola is well," Diego says.
I am very happy now.
After a little while, I end the call.
